cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SPECGAP, please cite it as below."
title: "SPECGAP: an open engine for assessing the coverage of public mass spectral libraries"
authors:
  - family-names: "Erumiseli"
    given-names: "Oshoma"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3813-4650"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Corvallis, Oregon, USA"
    email: "Erumiseli.oshomag@gmail.com"
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22653062"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Oshoma123/specgap"
abstract: >
  SPECGAP cross-matches natural-product structure sets (LOTUS, COCONUT)
  against the open spectral-library layer (GNPS, MassBank, MoNA), reporting
  structural coverage and name-recoverability. It parses the sources' native
  formats (MGF, MSP, GNPS JSON, MassBank records, SDF) and distinguishes
  structures that are genuinely uncovered from those that cannot be joined at
  all for want of a structure identifier.
